  user_input {
    user_response: "# MASTER PROMPT \342\200\224 REKAVANTA TECHNOLOGY & PRODUCT STUDIO\n\n## 1. ROLE & OBJECTIVE\n\nAct as a senior creative developer, award-winning digital art director, and expert frontend engineer.\n\nYour task is to build a premium, visually distinctive, single-file company profile landing page for **REKAVANTA**, a fictional technology and product studio.\n\nUse the supplied Orvante branding-agency design specification as the PRIMARY visual and structural reference.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- Do not copy the Orvante branding, business identity, or its agency-related content.\n- Reinterpret its visual language for a modern technology company.\n- Preserve its editorial composition, monochromatic art direction, asymmetrical layouts, typography scale, cinematic imagery, and sophisticated motion design.\n- The result must feel like a professionally art-directed technology studio website, NOT a generic SaaS landing page or AI-generated template.\n\nThe goal is to create an exceptional company profile website that communicates the company\'s identity, philosophy, business model, and selected initiatives.\n\n## 2. COMPANY IDENTITY\n\nCompany Name: REKAVANTA\n\nCompany Descriptor:\nTechnology & Product Studio\n\nTagline:\nBuild Solutions. Create Possibilities.\n\nIndustry:\nInformation Technology & Software Development.\n\nBusiness Model:\nHybrid Technology Company.\n\nREKAVANTA operates through two complementary business directions:\n\nA. DIGITAL SERVICES\n- Custom software development.\n- Website and web application development.\n- Mobile application development.\n- AI integration and intelligent systems.\n- Business process automation.\n- UI/UX engineering.\n\nB. INDEPENDENT DIGITAL PRODUCTS\n- SaaS platforms.\n- Proprietary software.\n- Digital productivity tools.\n- AI-powered applications.\n- Scalable digital products.\n\nCore Positioning:\n\nRekavanta is a technology and product studio that combines professional software development services with independent digital product development.\n\nThe company helps businesses and organizations solve real-world problems through technology while continuously exploring, engineering, and building its own digital products.\n\nBrand Philosophy:\n\nTechnology should do more than just work. It should solve problems, unlock possibilities, and create meaningful impact.\n\nBrand Personality:\n- Innovative.\n- Minimal.\n- Intelligent.\n- Precise.\n- Ambitious.\n- Professional.\n- Forward-thinking.\n\n## 3. DESIGN DIRECTION\n\nFollow the visual characteristics of the supplied Orvante reference.\n\nStyle:\n- Strict monochrome editorial design.\n- Premium creative studio aesthetic.\n- Minimalist but visually expressive.\n- Bold oversized typography.\n- Asymmetrical composition.\n- Cinematic editorial imagery.\n- Strong whitespace management.\n- High-contrast layouts.\n- Sophisticated motion design.\n\nColor Palette:\n\nHero:\n- Background: #DADADA\n- Primary text: #111111\n- Secondary surface: #CDCDCD\n\nLower Sections:\n- Background: #000000\n- Primary text: #F4F4F4\n- Secondary text: #A0A0A0\n- Muted text: #6F6F6F\n- Borders: rgba(255,255,255,0.14)\n\nBrand Accent:\n- Use a restrained cool electric blue accent such as #7DAFE0.\n- Only use it for meaningful interactive details, small status indicators, and selected highlights.\n- Do not introduce colorful gradients.\n\nTypography:\n- Inter Tight: body text, UI, labels, and navigation.\n- Archivo: oversized titles, brand identity, and editorial headlines.\n- Use variable font weights and widths where appropriate.\n\nTypography must feel intentional, bold, and carefully balanced.\n\nAvoid:\n- Generic startup landing page patterns.\n- Excessive gradients.\n- Excessive glassmorphism.\n- Unnecessary rounded cards.\n- Random decorative icons.\n- Excessive animations.\n- Generic AI-generated illustrations.\n- Unnecessary 3D effects.\n\nEvery element must have a clear visual or functional purpose.\n\n## 4. WEBSITE STRUCTURE\n\nBuild exactly THREE primary sections.\n\nSECTION 01 \342\200\224 HERO / COMPANY INTRODUCTION\n\nPurpose:\nIntroduce Rekavanta and establish its visual identity.\n\nLayout:\n- Large editorial hero composition.\n- Light grey background.\n- Navigation pill in the upper-left corner.\n- Contact action in the upper-right corner.\n- Large oversized headline on the left.\n- Cinematic central visual.\n- Brand identity plate integrated into the visual.\n- Supporting company introduction.\n- Small business information cards.\n- Additional visual information on the right side.\n\nMain Headline:\n\n\"BUILD\nWHAT\'S NEXT.\"\n\nBrand Plate:\nREKAVANTA\n\nCompany Descriptor:\nTECHNOLOGY & PRODUCT STUDIO\n\nHero Supporting Copy:\n\n\"We engineer digital solutions and build independent products that turn ambitious ideas into meaningful technology.\"\n\nAbout Label:\n(ABOUT REKAVANTA)\n\nShort Description:\n\n\"Combining software engineering, digital innovation, and intelligent technology to solve real-world problems.\"\n\nPrimary CTA:\nExplore Our Studio \342\206\227\n\nSecondary CTA:\nStart a Conversation \342\206\227\n\nHero Information Cards:\n\nCard 1:\n02+\nBusiness Directions\n\nCard 2:\n03\nSelected Initiatives\n\nThese numbers represent the company\'s two business directions and three showcased initiatives, NOT customer or performance statistics.\n\nNavigation:\n- Home\n- Studio\n- Work\n\nInclude a Contact button.\n\nNavigation should use an elegant sliding active pill interaction inspired by the reference.\n\nHero Visual:\n\nUse an original monochromatic editorial visual representing a fictional Asian technology founder or software engineer seen from behind, wearing modern technical clothing.\n\nThe visual should blend naturally into the light grey background.\n\nDo not reuse the original Orvante brand images, avatars, or assets unless specifically supplied as approved assets.\n\nIf image generation is available, create an original cinematic image.\n\nOtherwise, create a sophisticated abstract composition using CSS, inline SVG, and layered visual elements.\n\nDo not invent external image URLs.\n\nSupporting visual elements may include:\n- Small technical labels.\n- Thin lines.\n- Minimal graphical marks.\n- Product-oriented visual details.\n\nReplace Orvante\'s fictional partner logos with simple conceptual labels:\n\nSOFTWARE\nPRODUCTS\nINTELLIGENCE\n\nDo not create fake client logos.\n\nSECTION 02 \342\200\224 MANIFESTO / COMPANY PHILOSOPHY\n\nPurpose:\nCommunicate the company\'s philosophy and demonstrate its approach toward technology.\n\nUse a full-width pure black background.\n\nCreate a spacious editorial layout.\n\nMain Statement:\n\n\"Technology should do more than just work. It should solve problems, remove friction, unlock new possibilities, and turn ambitious ideas into meaningful digital products.\"\n\nThe entire statement must be centered and carefully distributed across approximately five lines.\n\nEvery word must have its own span.\n\nCreate a scroll-driven word-by-word color transition:\n- Initial text color: #6F6F6F.\n- Completed text color: #F4F4F4.\n- Use a smooth reading-order reveal.\n- Maintain a soft transition edge across approximately three words.\n\nSupporting Statement:\n\n\"From custom software solutions to independent digital products. Engineered with purpose. Built to evolve.\"\n\nAdd three small editorial labels:\n\nENGINEERING\nINNOVATION\nIMPACT\n\nThe section should feel like a brand manifesto rather than an ordinary paragraph section.\n\nSECTION 03 \342\200\224 OUR STUDIO / BUSINESS MODEL & SELECTED WORK\n\nPurpose:\nExplain what Rekavanta actually builds and demonstrate its business direction.\n\nUse a black background with a sophisticated bordered editorial panel.\n\nMain Heading:\n\n\"Two engines.\nOne direction.\"\n\nSupporting Copy:\n\n\"We combine professional technology services with independent product development, creating solutions that solve immediate challenges while building possibilities for the future.\"\n\nCreate two visually distinct business pillars.\n\nPILLAR 01 \342\200\224 DIGITAL SERVICES\n\nDescription:\n\n\"We design and engineer tailored digital solutions that help businesses and organizations operate, innovate, and grow.\"\n\nShow the following capabilities:\n- Software Development.\n- Web & Mobile Applications.\n- AI Integration.\n- Business Automation.\n- UI/UX Engineering.\n\nPILLAR 02 \342\200\224 DIGITAL PRODUCTS\n\nDescription:\n\n\"We explore, design, and develop independent digital products built to solve everyday problems and create long-term value.\"\n\nShow:\n- SaaS Platforms.\n- Business Applications.\n- Productivity Tools.\n- AI-powered Software.\n\nSELECTED INITIATIVES\n\nShowcase three selected initiatives using elegant editorial cards.\n\nPROJECT 01 \342\200\224 HUNI\n\nCategory:\nProperty Management / SaaS\n\nDescription:\n\n\"A digital property management platform designed to simplify boarding house operations, tenant management, billing, and reporting.\"\n\nStatus Label:\nPRODUCT CONCEPT\n\nPROJECT 02 \342\200\224 PERSONAL OS\n\nCategory:\nProductivity / Personal Software\n\nDescription:\n\n\"A personal productivity system designed to help individuals manage tasks, energy, goals, and daily progress.\"\n\nStatus Label:\nPRODUCT CONCEPT\n\nPROJECT 03 \342\200\224 SENTUL TREKKING INFORMATION SYSTEM\n\nCategory:\nCommunity Digitalization / Web Development\n\nDescription:\n\n\"A community-oriented information platform providing trekking destination information and booking contact access.\"\n\nStatus Label:\nCOMMUNITY PROJECT\n\nImportant:\n- These are selected initiatives, not claims of commercial success.\n- Never invent users, revenue, customers, project results, partnerships, or awards.\n- Clearly distinguish product concepts from actual community projects.\n\nFINAL CALL TO ACTION\n\nHeadline:\n\n\"Have an idea worth building?\"\n\nSupporting Copy:\n\n\"Let\'s explore how technology can turn your ideas into meaningful solutions.\"\n\nCTA:\nLet\'s Build Together \342\206\227\n\nInclude a minimal footer with:\n- REKAVANTA.\n- Technology & Product Studio.\n- Navigation links.\n- Contact information placeholders to be replaced with verified details.\n- Copyright.\n\n## 5. VISUAL COMPOSITION & ART DIRECTION\n\nDesktop target:\n1440px artboard.\n\nUse a design scale based on:\n\nu = min(100vw / 1440, 1.333px)\n\nHero target height:\nApproximately 938u.\n\nFollow the original reference\'s general composition:\n- Navigation around the upper-left region.\n- Large editorial headline aligned to the left.\n- Central hero visual.\n- Brand plate integrated into the visual.\n- Small informational cards.\n- Right-side supporting elements.\n- Horizontal visual separation before the manifesto.\n\nDo not force every element to use exact reference coordinates if doing so compromises the Rekavanta content.\n\nUse intentional spacing, precise alignments, visual hierarchy, and balanced asymmetry.\n\nThe design must look coherent at 1440px and remain functional at smaller widths.\n\n## 6. MOTION & INTERACTIONS\n\nImplement motion using vanilla JavaScript and the Web Animations API where appropriate.\n\nPAGE LOAD:\n- Hero headline rises from clipped masks.\n- Hero visual fades in and moves upward slightly.\n- Navigation enters elegantly.\n- Supporting content appears with subtle staggered transitions.\n- Brand plate fades in.\n- Avoid excessive bounce effects.\n\nNAVIGATION:\n- Sliding active pill.\n- Smooth anchor navigation.\n- Elegant hover states.\n\nHERO:\n- Subtle parallax movement on the hero visual.\n- Buttons lift approximately 1px on hover.\n- Small progress indicators animate naturally.\n\nMANIFESTO:\n- Word-by-word grey-to-white scroll reveal.\n- Use IntersectionObserver or scroll progress calculations efficiently.\n\nSTUDIO:\n- Cards rise slightly on hover.\n- Borders and subtle accents respond to interaction.\n- Project visual elements receive minimal hover transitions.\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n- Support prefers-reduced-motion.\n- Provide visible keyboard focus styles.\n- Use semantic HTML.\n- Ensure sufficient text contrast.\n- Do not make essential content depend on animation.\n\nIf the page is opened with ?rec=1, optionally use time-based animation so the major visual states can be captured without scrolling.\n\n## 7. RESPONSIVE DESIGN\n\nDesktop:\n- Maintain the editorial asymmetric composition.\n- Use the full-width hero layout.\n- Keep text and media balanced.\n\nTablet:\n- Adjust typography and spacing.\n- Preserve visual hierarchy.\n- Reduce unnecessary overlapping elements.\n\nMobile (maximum 760px):\n- Single-column layout.\n- Compact navigation.\n- Contact becomes a compact icon/button.\n- Headline appears before the hero visual.\n- Hero visual uses full available width.\n- Supporting information cards become a compact grid.\n- Manifesto font size adapts to the viewport.\n- Business pillars stack vertically.\n- Project cards become vertically arranged.\n- Footer remains minimal.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- No horizontal overflow.\n- No clipped text.\n- No overlapping navigation.\n- All buttons remain accessible.\n- Maintain visual quality rather than simply shrinking the desktop design.\n\n## 8. TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS\n\nBuild the complete website in ONE SINGLE HTML FILE.\n\nFilename:\nindex.html\n\nTechnology:\n- HTML5.\n- CSS3.\n- Vanilla JavaScript.\n\nStrict restrictions:\n- No React.\n- No Vue.\n- No Angular.\n- No Tailwind CSS.\n- No Bootstrap.\n- No external JavaScript frameworks.\n- No build tools.\n- No unnecessary dependencies.\n\nUse:\n- Embedded CSS inside <style>.\n- Embedded JavaScript inside <script>.\n- Inline SVG for custom icons and graphical details.\n- CSS Grid and Flexbox for layouts.\n- CSS variables for design tokens.\n\nGoogle Fonts may be loaded through their stylesheet.\n\nThe page must run directly by opening index.html in a browser.\n\nWrite clean, readable, maintainable code with logical sections and meaningful comments.\n\nUse semantic HTML elements.\n\nOptimize:\n- Image loading.\n- Animation performance.\n- Event handling.\n- Responsive rendering.\n- Scroll event efficiency.\n\nDo not create non-functional interactive controls.\n\n## 9. CONTENT & BRAND INTEGRITY\n\nThe entire website must consistently represent Rekavanta.\n\nDo not leave:\n- Orvante references.\n- Branding-agency terminology.\n- Fictional client testimonials.\n- Fake company statistics.\n- Fake customer logos.\n- Invented addresses.\n- Invented awards.\n- Unsupported commercial achievements.\n\nDo not change the core identity, business model, tagline, or selected project information.\n\nUse precise, professional English throughout the website.\n\n## 10. FINAL ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA\n\nThe implementation is successful only when:\n\n1. The page visually follows the supplied Orvante reference\'s editorial direction.\n2. The Rekavanta brand identity is clearly established.\n3. The website communicates the hybrid technology business model.\n4. All three primary sections are complete.\n5. The hero composition feels cinematic and professionally art-directed.\n6. The manifesto has a working scroll-driven word reveal.\n7. The final studio section clearly presents services, products, and initiatives.\n8. Animations are smooth and intentional.\n9. Responsive behavior works on desktop, tablet, and mobile.\n10. There are no broken links, console errors, or horizontal overflow.\n11. The source is contained in a single index.html file.\n12. The final result does not look like a generic AI-generated website.\n\n## 11. EXECUTION INSTRUCTIONS\n\nDo not merely describe the design.\n\nActually implement the complete website.\n\nBefore finishing:\n- Inspect the HTML structure.\n- Review CSS consistency.\n- Test JavaScript interactions.\n- Check mobile responsiveness.\n- Verify all three sections.\n- Fix visual and functional issues.\n\nPrioritize design quality, implementation quality, and brand consistency.\n\nDeliver the complete, functional index.html source code."
    items {
      text: "# MASTER PROMPT \342\200\224 REKAVANTA TECHNOLOGY & PRODUCT STUDIO\n\n## 1. ROLE & OBJECTIVE\n\nAct as a senior creative developer, award-winning digital art director, and expert frontend engineer.\n\nYour task is to build a premium, visually distinctive, single-file company profile landing page for **REKAVANTA**, a fictional technology and product studio.\n\nUse the supplied Orvante branding-agency design specification as the PRIMARY visual and structural reference.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- Do not copy the Orvante branding, business identity, or its agency-related content.\n- Reinterpret its visual language for a modern technology company.\n- Preserve its editorial composition, monochromatic art direction, asymmetrical layouts, typography scale, cinematic imagery, and sophisticated motion design.\n- The result must feel like a professionally art-directed technology studio website, NOT a generic SaaS landing page or AI-generated template.\n\nThe goal is to create an exceptional company profile website that communicates the company\'s identity, philosophy, business model, and selected initiatives.\n\n## 2. COMPANY IDENTITY\n\nCompany Name: REKAVANTA\n\nCompany Descriptor:\nTechnology & Product Studio\n\nTagline:\nBuild Solutions. Create Possibilities.\n\nIndustry:\nInformation Technology & Software Development.\n\nBusiness Model:\nHybrid Technology Company.\n\nREKAVANTA operates through two complementary business directions:\n\nA. DIGITAL SERVICES\n- Custom software development.\n- Website and web application development.\n- Mobile application development.\n- AI integration and intelligent systems.\n- Business process automation.\n- UI/UX engineering.\n\nB. INDEPENDENT DIGITAL PRODUCTS\n- SaaS platforms.\n- Proprietary software.\n- Digital productivity tools.\n- AI-powered applications.\n- Scalable digital products.\n\nCore Positioning:\n\nRekavanta is a technology and product studio that combines professional software development services with independent digital product development.\n\nThe company helps businesses and organizations solve real-world problems through technology while continuously exploring, engineering, and building its own digital products.\n\nBrand Philosophy:\n\nTechnology should do more than just work. It should solve problems, unlock possibilities, and create meaningful impact.\n\nBrand Personality:\n- Innovative.\n- Minimal.\n- Intelligent.\n- Precise.\n- Ambitious.\n- Professional.\n- Forward-thinking.\n\n## 3. DESIGN DIRECTION\n\nFollow the visual characteristics of the supplied Orvante reference.\n\nStyle:\n- Strict monochrome editorial design.\n- Premium creative studio aesthetic.\n- Minimalist but visually expressive.\n- Bold oversized typography.\n- Asymmetrical composition.\n- Cinematic editorial imagery.\n- Strong whitespace management.\n- High-contrast layouts.\n- Sophisticated motion design.\n\nColor Palette:\n\nHero:\n- Background: #DADADA\n- Primary text: #111111\n- Secondary surface: #CDCDCD\n\nLower Sections:\n- Background: #000000\n- Primary text: #F4F4F4\n- Secondary text: #A0A0A0\n- Muted text: #6F6F6F\n- Borders: rgba(255,255,255,0.14)\n\nBrand Accent:\n- Use a restrained cool electric blue accent such as #7DAFE0.\n- Only use it for meaningful interactive details, small status indicators, and selected highlights.\n- Do not introduce colorful gradients.\n\nTypography:\n- Inter Tight: body text, UI, labels, and navigation.\n- Archivo: oversized titles, brand identity, and editorial headlines.\n- Use variable font weights and widths where appropriate.\n\nTypography must feel intentional, bold, and carefully balanced.\n\nAvoid:\n- Generic startup landing page patterns.\n- Excessive gradients.\n- Excessive glassmorphism.\n- Unnecessary rounded cards.\n- Random decorative icons.\n- Excessive animations.\n- Generic AI-generated illustrations.\n- Unnecessary 3D effects.\n\nEvery element must have a clear visual or functional purpose.\n\n## 4. WEBSITE STRUCTURE\n\nBuild exactly THREE primary sections.\n\nSECTION 01 \342\200\224 HERO / COMPANY INTRODUCTION\n\nPurpose:\nIntroduce Rekavanta and establish its visual identity.\n\nLayout:\n- Large editorial hero composition.\n- Light grey background.\n- Navigation pill in the upper-left corner.\n- Contact action in the upper-right corner.\n- Large oversized headline on the left.\n- Cinematic central visual.\n- Brand identity plate integrated into the visual.\n- Supporting company introduction.\n- Small business information cards.\n- Additional visual information on the right side.\n\nMain Headline:\n\n\"BUILD\nWHAT\'S NEXT.\"\n\nBrand Plate:\nREKAVANTA\n\nCompany Descriptor:\nTECHNOLOGY & PRODUCT STUDIO\n\nHero Supporting Copy:\n\n\"We engineer digital solutions and build independent products that turn ambitious ideas into meaningful technology.\"\n\nAbout Label:\n(ABOUT REKAVANTA)\n\nShort Description:\n\n\"Combining software engineering, digital innovation, and intelligent technology to solve real-world problems.\"\n\nPrimary CTA:\nExplore Our Studio \342\206\227\n\nSecondary CTA:\nStart a Conversation \342\206\227\n\nHero Information Cards:\n\nCard 1:\n02+\nBusiness Directions\n\nCard 2:\n03\nSelected Initiatives\n\nThese numbers represent the company\'s two business directions and three showcased initiatives, NOT customer or performance statistics.\n\nNavigation:\n- Home\n- Studio\n- Work\n\nInclude a Contact button.\n\nNavigation should use an elegant sliding active pill interaction inspired by the reference.\n\nHero Visual:\n\nUse an original monochromatic editorial visual representing a fictional Asian technology founder or software engineer seen from behind, wearing modern technical clothing.\n\nThe visual should blend naturally into the light grey background.\n\nDo not reuse the original Orvante brand images, avatars, or assets unless specifically supplied as approved assets.\n\nIf image generation is available, create an original cinematic image.\n\nOtherwise, create a sophisticated abstract composition using CSS, inline SVG, and layered visual elements.\n\nDo not invent external image URLs.\n\nSupporting visual elements may include:\n- Small technical labels.\n- Thin lines.\n- Minimal graphical marks.\n- Product-oriented visual details.\n\nReplace Orvante\'s fictional partner logos with simple conceptual labels:\n\nSOFTWARE\nPRODUCTS\nINTELLIGENCE\n\nDo not create fake client logos.\n\nSECTION 02 \342\200\224 MANIFESTO / COMPANY PHILOSOPHY\n\nPurpose:\nCommunicate the company\'s philosophy and demonstrate its approach toward technology.\n\nUse a full-width pure black background.\n\nCreate a spacious editorial layout.\n\nMain Statement:\n\n\"Technology should do more than just work. It should solve problems, remove friction, unlock new possibilities, and turn ambitious ideas into meaningful digital products.\"\n\nThe entire statement must be centered and carefully distributed across approximately five lines.\n\nEvery word must have its own span.\n\nCreate a scroll-driven word-by-word color transition:\n- Initial text color: #6F6F6F.\n- Completed text color: #F4F4F4.\n- Use a smooth reading-order reveal.\n- Maintain a soft transition edge across approximately three words.\n\nSupporting Statement:\n\n\"From custom software solutions to independent digital products. Engineered with purpose. Built to evolve.\"\n\nAdd three small editorial labels:\n\nENGINEERING\nINNOVATION\nIMPACT\n\nThe section should feel like a brand manifesto rather than an ordinary paragraph section.\n\nSECTION 03 \342\200\224 OUR STUDIO / BUSINESS MODEL & SELECTED WORK\n\nPurpose:\nExplain what Rekavanta actually builds and demonstrate its business direction.\n\nUse a black background with a sophisticated bordered editorial panel.\n\nMain Heading:\n\n\"Two engines.\nOne direction.\"\n\nSupporting Copy:\n\n\"We combine professional technology services with independent product development, creating solutions that solve immediate challenges while building possibilities for the future.\"\n\nCreate two visually distinct business pillars.\n\nPILLAR 01 \342\200\224 DIGITAL SERVICES\n\nDescription:\n\n\"We design and engineer tailored digital solutions that help businesses and organizations operate, innovate, and grow.\"\n\nShow the following capabilities:\n- Software Development.\n- Web & Mobile Applications.\n- AI Integration.\n- Business Automation.\n- UI/UX Engineering.\n\nPILLAR 02 \342\200\224 DIGITAL PRODUCTS\n\nDescription:\n\n\"We explore, design, and develop independent digital products built to solve everyday problems and create long-term value.\"\n\nShow:\n- SaaS Platforms.\n- Business Applications.\n- Productivity Tools.\n- AI-powered Software.\n\nSELECTED INITIATIVES\n\nShowcase three selected initiatives using elegant editorial cards.\n\nPROJECT 01 \342\200\224 HUNI\n\nCategory:\nProperty Management / SaaS\n\nDescription:\n\n\"A digital property management platform designed to simplify boarding house operations, tenant management, billing, and reporting.\"\n\nStatus Label:\nPRODUCT CONCEPT\n\nPROJECT 02 \342\200\224 PERSONAL OS\n\nCategory:\nProductivity / Personal Software\n\nDescription:\n\n\"A personal productivity system designed to help individuals manage tasks, energy, goals, and daily progress.\"\n\nStatus Label:\nPRODUCT CONCEPT\n\nPROJECT 03 \342\200\224 SENTUL TREKKING INFORMATION SYSTEM\n\nCategory:\nCommunity Digitalization / Web Development\n\nDescription:\n\n\"A community-oriented information platform providing trekking destination information and booking contact access.\"\n\nStatus Label:\nCOMMUNITY PROJECT\n\nImportant:\n- These are selected initiatives, not claims of commercial success.\n- Never invent users, revenue, customers, project results, partnerships, or awards.\n- Clearly distinguish product concepts from actual community projects.\n\nFINAL CALL TO ACTION\n\nHeadline:\n\n\"Have an idea worth building?\"\n\nSupporting Copy:\n\n\"Let\'s explore how technology can turn your ideas into meaningful solutions.\"\n\nCTA:\nLet\'s Build Together \342\206\227\n\nInclude a minimal footer with:\n- REKAVANTA.\n- Technology & Product Studio.\n- Navigation links.\n- Contact information placeholders to be replaced with verified details.\n- Copyright.\n\n## 5. VISUAL COMPOSITION & ART DIRECTION\n\nDesktop target:\n1440px artboard.\n\nUse a design scale based on:\n\nu = min(100vw / 1440, 1.333px)\n\nHero target height:\nApproximately 938u.\n\nFollow the original reference\'s general composition:\n- Navigation around the upper-left region.\n- Large editorial headline aligned to the left.\n- Central hero visual.\n- Brand plate integrated into the visual.\n- Small informational cards.\n- Right-side supporting elements.\n- Horizontal visual separation before the manifesto.\n\nDo not force every element to use exact reference coordinates if doing so compromises the Rekavanta content.\n\nUse intentional spacing, precise alignments, visual hierarchy, and balanced asymmetry.\n\nThe design must look coherent at 1440px and remain functional at smaller widths.\n\n## 6. MOTION & INTERACTIONS\n\nImplement motion using vanilla JavaScript and the Web Animations API where appropriate.\n\nPAGE LOAD:\n- Hero headline rises from clipped masks.\n- Hero visual fades in and moves upward slightly.\n- Navigation enters elegantly.\n- Supporting content appears with subtle staggered transitions.\n- Brand plate fades in.\n- Avoid excessive bounce effects.\n\nNAVIGATION:\n- Sliding active pill.\n- Smooth anchor navigation.\n- Elegant hover states.\n\nHERO:\n- Subtle parallax movement on the hero visual.\n- Buttons lift approximately 1px on hover.\n- Small progress indicators animate naturally.\n\nMANIFESTO:\n- Word-by-word grey-to-white scroll reveal.\n- Use IntersectionObserver or scroll progress calculations efficiently.\n\nSTUDIO:\n- Cards rise slightly on hover.\n- Borders and subtle accents respond to interaction.\n- Project visual elements receive minimal hover transitions.\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n- Support prefers-reduced-motion.\n- Provide visible keyboard focus styles.\n- Use semantic HTML.\n- Ensure sufficient text contrast.\n- Do not make essential content depend on animation.\n\nIf the page is opened with ?rec=1, optionally use time-based animation so the major visual states can be captured without scrolling.\n\n## 7. RESPONSIVE DESIGN\n\nDesktop:\n- Maintain the editorial asymmetric composition.\n- Use the full-width hero layout.\n- Keep text and media balanced.\n\nTablet:\n- Adjust typography and spacing.\n- Preserve visual hierarchy.\n- Reduce unnecessary overlapping elements.\n\nMobile (maximum 760px):\n- Single-column layout.\n- Compact navigation.\n- Contact becomes a compact icon/button.\n- Headline appears before the hero visual.\n- Hero visual uses full available width.\n- Supporting information cards become a compact grid.\n- Manifesto font size adapts to the viewport.\n- Business pillars stack vertically.\n- Project cards become vertically arranged.\n- Footer remains minimal.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- No horizontal overflow.\n- No clipped text.\n- No overlapping navigation.\n- All buttons remain accessible.\n- Maintain visual quality rather than simply shrinking the desktop design.\n\n## 8. TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS\n\nBuild the complete website in ONE SINGLE HTML FILE.\n\nFilename:\nindex.html\n\nTechnology:\n- HTML5.\n- CSS3.\n- Vanilla JavaScript.\n\nStrict restrictions:\n- No React.\n- No Vue.\n- No Angular.\n- No Tailwind CSS.\n- No Bootstrap.\n- No external JavaScript frameworks.\n- No build tools.\n- No unnecessary dependencies.\n\nUse:\n- Embedded CSS inside <style>.\n- Embedded JavaScript inside <script>.\n- Inline SVG for custom icons and graphical details.\n- CSS Grid and Flexbox for layouts.\n- CSS variables for design tokens.\n\nGoogle Fonts may be loaded through their stylesheet.\n\nThe page must run directly by opening index.html in a browser.\n\nWrite clean, readable, maintainable code with logical sections and meaningful comments.\n\nUse semantic HTML elements.\n\nOptimize:\n- Image loading.\n- Animation performance.\n- Event handling.\n- Responsive rendering.\n- Scroll event efficiency.\n\nDo not create non-functional interactive controls.\n\n## 9. CONTENT & BRAND INTEGRITY\n\nThe entire website must consistently represent Rekavanta.\n\nDo not leave:\n- Orvante references.\n- Branding-agency terminology.\n- Fictional client testimonials.\n- Fake company statistics.\n- Fake customer logos.\n- Invented addresses.\n- Invented awards.\n- Unsupported commercial achievements.\n\nDo not change the core identity, business model, tagline, or selected project information.\n\nUse precise, professional English throughout the website.\n\n## 10. FINAL ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA\n\nThe implementation is successful only when:\n\n1. The page visually follows the supplied Orvante reference\'s editorial direction.\n2. The Rekavanta brand identity is clearly established.\n3. The website communicates the hybrid technology business model.\n4. All three primary sections are complete.\n5. The hero composition feels cinematic and professionally art-directed.\n6. The manifesto has a working scroll-driven word reveal.\n7. The final studio section clearly presents services, products, and initiatives.\n8. Animations are smooth and intentional.\n9. Responsive behavior works on desktop, tablet, and mobile.\n10. There are no broken links, console errors, or horizontal overflow.\n11. The source is contained in a single index.html file.\n12. The final result does not look like a generic AI-generated website.\n\n## 11. EXECUTION INSTRUCTIONS\n\nDo not merely describe the design.\n\nActually implement the complete website.\n\nBefore finishing:\n- Inspect the HTML structure.\n- Review CSS consistency.\n- Test JavaScript interactions.\n- Check mobile responsiveness.\n- Verify all three sections.\n- Fix visual and functional issues.\n\nPrioritize design quality, implementation quality, and brand consistency.\n\nDeliver the complete, functional index.html source code."
    }
  }
}
