  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Image\'s Aesthetic**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the generated portrait and it perfectly embodies the Orvante-inspired monochromatic editorial aesthetic I was aiming for. The East Asian technology founder, viewed from a three-quarter back angle, in a matte charcoal technical jacket against a studio backdrop, is an exact visual match!\n\n\n**Verifying User Journeys**\n\nI\'m now focused on the interactive components, specifically navigation and scroll-driven word reveals. I\'ve designed smooth animations for pill switching and corresponding section scrolls. The manifesto\'s word reveal, transitioning text colors as it appears, is another key area I am confirming. Both are crucial to my vision.\n\n\n**Examining Interactive Elements**\n\nI\'m currently delving into the interactive Studio Initiative inspection and the Contact conversation drawer. Clicking an initiative now reveals detailed architecture notes and scope information, along with options to initiate a pre-contextualized conversation. The Contact features, including the accessible inquiry drawer and form validation, are also critical.\n\n\n**Defining Page Composition**\n\nI\'m now outlining the landing page layout. I envision an oversized headline, a central portrait with the brand identity, and supporting copy on the right. I\'m focusing on the \"About\" block with call-to-actions, and incorporating information cards for key areas like \"Business Directions\" and \"Selected Initiatives,\" along with conceptual labels. This will establish a strong visual foundation.\n\n\n**Defining Business Pillars**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the structure of the business pillars, which includes distinguishing two major areas: Digital Services and Digital Products. I am organizing their associated capabilities and product areas to ensure clarity. I\'m also planning the presentation of the three selected initiatives, interactive specifications and a final call to action to move users along the funnel. I\'ve got to plan for a minimal footer, of course.\n\n\n**Confirming HTML5 Structure**\n\nI\'m verifying how Vite serves a self-contained HTML5 `index.html`. It appears Vite handles the document directly at `http://localhost:3000` and bundles it into `dist/index.html`. My next step is checking to see whether I can unit-test pure logic from `src/utils/studioLogic.ts` and ensure that all math is working. I am setting the application name and description using `replace_file_content` on `/metadata.json`.\n\n\n"
