  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Scroll Indication**\n\nI\'m focusing on crafting a top-fixed, white progress bar to represent scroll position on the landing page. It needs to be lightweight and performant, ensuring it doesn\'t drag down the experience. I\'m keen on a visually clean execution.\n\n\n**Implementing Scroll Progress**\n\nI\'ve just added a helper function, `computePageScrollProgress`, along with a unit test. Now I\'m integrating a top-fixed progress bar into the HTML. I\'m focusing on a clean, performant design: a translucent track with a white progress bar. This bar will use `transform: scaleX()` for smooth updates during scroll, orchestrated through a `requestAnimationFrame`-throttled loop. Zero layout thrashing is key here.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_9510417955004774622"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Add computePageScrollProgress utility function to studioLogic.ts\", \"EndLine\":23, \"Instruction\":\"Add computePageScrollProgress function below clamp in /src/utils/studioLogic.ts\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"export function clamp(val: number, min: number, max: number): number {\\n  return Math.max(min, Math.min(max, val));\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Computes normalized page scroll progress in [0..1] given current scrollY,\\n * document scrollHeight, and viewport innerHeight.\\n */\\nexport function computePageScrollProgress(\\n  scrollY: number,\\n  docScrollHeight: number,\\n  viewportHeight: number\\n): number {\\n  const maxScroll = docScrollHeight - viewportHeight;\\n  if (maxScroll <= 0) return 0;\\n  return clamp(scrollY / maxScroll, 0, 1);\\n}\", \"StartLine\":18, \"TargetContent\":\"export function clamp(val: number, min: number, max: number): number {\\n  return Math.max(min, Math.min(max, val));\\n}\", \"TargetFile\":\"/src/utils/studioLogic.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Adding scroll progress calculation to studioLogic.ts\", \"toolSummary\":\"Add computePageScrollProgress utility\"}"
