    response: "I have implemented a thin (`3px`), white scroll progress bar fixed at the top edge of the page.\n\n### Summary of Implementation & Verification\n\n- **Fixed Top Scroll Progress Bar**:\n  - Added an accessible `role=\"progressbar\"` track (`#page-scroll-progress-track`) fixed at `top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; height: 3px` with a white fill bar (`#page-scroll-progress-bar`, `#ffffff`).\n- **Scroll Performance Optimization**:\n  - Uses GPU-composited `transform: scaleX(...)` with `transform-origin: left center` and `will-change: transform` instead of animating `width`, preventing layout recalculations.\n  - Updates inside the existing `requestAnimationFrame`-throttled passive `scroll` and `resize` listener loop (`onScrollUpdate`).\n- **Verification**:\n  - **Unit Tests**: Added `computePageScrollProgress` unit tests (`4/4` passing via `node:test`).\n  - **Browser Verification**: Confirmed initial state (`scaleX(0)` at `scrollY = 0`) and mid-scroll progression (`scaleX(0.3758)` / `aria-valuenow=\"38\"` at `1100px` scroll) at `1440\303\227900` with zero console errors."
